{%- comment -%}
  fye-carat-stepper — step to the next carat up or down in this design family.

  Built 01/09/2026, W916. Rendered INSIDE the buy box by main-product, not as
  a section: this is a size selector for a choice the shopper has already
  made, so it belongs with metal and quality, not with the merchandising rows
  below.

  NOT "ring size". FYE rings already have a finger-size option (A to Z+6) and
  two scales called the same thing on one page would confuse shoppers and
  staff alike. The words used here are CARAT and CENTRE STONE, never "size".

  ── THE DATA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

      fye.family        list.product_reference, plain namespace, so dot
                        notation is fine here (unlike the Search & Discovery
                        fields the sibling sections read — those need
                        brackets; see fye-related-products)
      fye.family_carat  number_decimal, the label for each entry

  The family list INCLUDES THE CURRENT PRODUCT, deliberately: every member
  carries an identical list, so this finds its own index and reads off the
  neighbours rather than reconstructing a ladder. Self is not filtered out
  before the index is found — doing so would shift every position by one.

  **The label comes from fye.family_carat, never filters.centre_weight.**
  Measured 01/09/2026: centre_weight is null on 64% of rings, including every
  eternity ring sampled, and where present it sometimes holds TOTAL diamond
  weight instead of the centre stone. A stepper labelled from it renders
  ladders like 0.33 -> 0.95 -> 1.2 -> 0.9, which is neither ascending nor
  true. family_carat is written from the same Gemex figure the import sorted
  the ladder by, so the label and the order cannot disagree.

  ── WHAT RENDERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    middle of the ladder   both controls
    smallest in family     larger only
    largest in family      smaller only
    no family, or fewer
    than 2 live members    NOTHING — no shell, no heading, no hidden element

  There is no disabled state and no arrow that goes nowhere. An absent
  stepper is correct for the ~1,000 one-off rings.

  ── HOLES IN THE LADDER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

  product_reference keeps pointing at deleted products, so a neighbour can be
  nil even though the import dropped dead references at generation time. The
  single pass below therefore takes the NEAREST LIVE entry either side rather
  than the immediate index — a hole in the middle of a family steps over
  itself instead of hiding the control.

  ── TIES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  336 families hold two members at the same carat; the import breaks ties by
  model code so the order is stable, but "Larger 1ct" on a ring that is itself
  1ct reads as a bug. Where the neighbour's carat equals the current one the
  control says "Another option" instead of a direction — same shape, so the
  row does not shift. Its arrow is dropped too: there is no direction to point
  in when the weight is identical.

  ── ARROWS, NOT CHEVRONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Ed, 01/09/2026. UP AND DOWN rather than left and right, because a carat
  ladder is a scale rather than a sequence: "larger" is up whichever side of
  the row the control happens to sit on. Left/right would also collide with
  the browser's own back/forward sense, and every one of these controls is a
  real page navigation.

  They come from the icon snippet (`arrow-up` / `arrow-down`, added to it in
  the same change) rather than inline SVG or a Unicode glyph — the brand
  permits only two glyphs, `›` and the middot, and the theme already has one
  icon system that owns stroke weight and caps.

  Each arrow sits on the OUTER edge of its control, so the pair points away
  from the current weight in the middle.

  Parameters:
    product — required
    scale   — "Centre stone" (default) or "Diamond weight" on eternity
              templates, where the ladder is total diamond weight
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign p = product
  assign scale_label = scale | default: 'Centre stone'
  assign scale_words = scale_label | downcase

  assign fam = p.metafields.fye.family.value

  comment
    Find the current product's own index first. Everything else is relative
    to it, so a product missing from its own list renders nothing rather than
    guessing a position.
  endcomment
  assign idx = -1
  if fam != blank
    for m in fam
      if m != blank and m.handle == p.handle
        assign idx = forloop.index0
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    One pass for both neighbours. `smaller` keeps being overwritten by later
    entries below the index, so it ends up holding the NEAREST one; `larger`
    is only assigned once, so it holds the nearest above.
  endcomment
  assign smaller = nil
  assign larger = nil

  if idx >= 0
    for m in fam
      unless m == blank or m.handle == p.handle
        if forloop.index0 < idx
          assign smaller = m
        elsif larger == nil
          assign larger = m
        endif
      endunless
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if smaller != nil or larger != nil -%}
  {%- liquid
    capture now_ct
      render 'fye-carat-label', value: p.metafields.fye.family_carat.value
    endcapture
    capture small_ct
      render 'fye-carat-label', value: smaller.metafields.fye.family_carat.value
    endcapture
    capture large_ct
      render 'fye-carat-label', value: larger.metafields.fye.family_carat.value
    endcapture

    assign now_ct = now_ct | strip
    assign small_ct = small_ct | strip
    assign large_ct = large_ct | strip

    comment
      A neighbour at the same weight is not "smaller" or "larger".
    endcomment
    assign small_tied = false
    if small_ct != blank and small_ct == now_ct
      assign small_tied = true
    endif
    assign large_tied = false
    if large_ct != blank and large_ct == now_ct
      assign large_tied = true
    endif
  -%}

  <nav class="pdp__field cstep" aria-label="{{ scale_label | escape }} options">
    <p class="pdp__label pdp__label--inline">
      {{ scale_label }}
      {%- if now_ct != blank -%}
        <span class="pdp__labelval">{{ now_ct }}ct</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>

    <div class="cstep__row">
      {%- if smaller != nil -%}
        {%- liquid
          if small_tied
            assign small_dir = 'Another option'
            assign small_aria = 'Another ' | append: scale_words | append: ' at ' | append: small_ct | append: ' carat'
          elsif small_ct == blank
            assign small_dir = 'Smaller'
            assign small_aria = 'Smaller ' | append: scale_words
          else
            assign small_dir = 'Smaller'
            assign small_aria = 'Smaller ' | append: scale_words | append: ', ' | append: small_ct | append: ' carat'
          endif
        -%}
        <a class="cstep__opt cstep__opt--down"
           href="{{ smaller.url }}"
           aria-label="{{ small_aria | escape }}">
          {%- unless small_tied -%}
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-down', size: 16 -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
          <span class="cstep__txt">
            <span class="cstep__dir">{{ small_dir }}</span>
            {%- if small_ct != blank -%}
              <span class="cstep__ct">{{ small_ct }}ct</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The current weight, between the two. Static text, never a link — a
        control that returns you to the page you are on is noise.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if now_ct != blank -%}
        <span class="cstep__now" aria-hidden="true">{{ now_ct }}ct</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if larger != nil -%}
        {%- liquid
          if large_tied
            assign large_dir = 'Another option'
            assign large_aria = 'Another ' | append: scale_words | append: ' at ' | append: large_ct | append: ' carat'
          elsif large_ct == blank
            assign large_dir = 'Larger'
            assign large_aria = 'Larger ' | append: scale_words
          else
            assign large_dir = 'Larger'
            assign large_aria = 'Larger ' | append: scale_words | append: ', ' | append: large_ct | append: ' carat'
          endif
        -%}
        <a class="cstep__opt cstep__opt--up"
           href="{{ larger.url }}"
           aria-label="{{ large_aria | escape }}">
          {%- unless large_tied -%}
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-up', size: 16 -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
          <span class="cstep__txt">
            <span class="cstep__dir">{{ large_dir }}</span>
            {%- if large_ct != blank -%}
              <span class="cstep__ct">{{ large_ct }}ct</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}
